  "notes": "The avenue from East View Avenue east to Fergus Street (y about 800-860) carries only the word AVENUE in this strip: recorded as '?'. The 60 ft street running west from Haight Avenue at y 2900 toward Hamilton Avenue is lettered only AVENUE: '?' (in line with Bruce Avenue, probably Bruce). Thompson Heights Avenue: name printed along its diagonal part west of the strip, only AVE. inside it. The diagonal street with 43xx house numbers from the top-left to Pullan Avenue is lettered HAIGHT AVE. north-west of the strip. Pullan Avenue: name printed west of Hamilton Avenue; only AVENUE printed east of it. The street along the bottom edge is lettered only AVENUE (far east): taken as Chase Avenue, not read off the plate; the plate is cut along its south side, with stubs of streets going south at x about 5730, 5990 (Hamilton), 6225, 6740 (Langland), 6958 and 7520 (Fergus). Craven, Rodney: no suffix seen. Apjones: suffix not seen, Street assumed. Addingham Place is one curving street (Addingham along the east-west leg, Place along the north-south leg). Langland south of the '?' avenue narrows to a 30 ft strip beside an orange boundary band. Fergus Street between Rodney and Pullan is lettered ST. only. A narrow grey-banded strip west of Hamilton Avenue at y about 4583 was read as a boundary, not a street. Fergus/Rodney is an L corner."
